Mode        Meaning
----        -------
x           Operate on x units (chars. or lines).  Default is 1.

x-y         Operate on a range of units.  Note that a '.' can be used in
            place of either x or y to indicate the current position.  A '>'
            can be used in place of y to indicate the last position.  For
            example, the range '.->' means do the command on everything 
            from the current position to the end of the line or file.

x@y         Operate on x units, starting at unit y

@x          Similar to x@y, but only operate on 1 unit.  In case of
            '>' and '<', this mode will move the character pointer to the
            specified position.

<filename>  An optional filename may be specified.

<string>    A string argument may be specified.  Also see the help on strings.
